{"term":"cripple","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:1c54393608738ca413","definition":"Crippled.","example":"And chide the cripple tardy-gaited night, who, like a foul and ugly witch, doth limp so tediously away.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic, dated, not-comparable","register":"archaic, dated, not-comparable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cripple#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f722b4ae39b16e0f48","definition":"A person who has severely impaired physical abilities because of deformation, injury, or amputation of parts of the body.","example":"He returned from war a cripple.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["disabled"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"offensive","register":"countable, offensive, uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cripple#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:84624882663851e557","definition":"A person who is severely impaired or deficient in some non-physical way.","example":"Many a one, who perhaps doesn't suspect it, is a moral cripple, or maybe a mental cripple.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"broadly, figuratively","register":"broadly, countable, figuratively, uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cripple#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4a72d7566ab2ea44a3","definition":"A shortened wooden stud or brace used to construct the portion of a wall above a door or above and below a window.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.o